<title>UK: Vodafone up on takeover talk, call buying.</title>
<headline>Vodafone up on takeover talk, call buying.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Vodafone climbed to a two-month high on Wednesday amid rumours that U.S. telecommunications giant AT&amp;T Corp is contemplating a bid for the UK concern, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 0944 GMT, the shares were up 10-1/2p to 244p.  </p>
<p>&quot;I think it's very unlikely, but the rumours are helping to get things going,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Heavy buying of Vodafone call options also contributed to the advance, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares rose yesterday after brokerage ABN AMRO Hoare Govett reiterated a buy recommendation, they said.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
